 extension, suggesting the market is not fighting the prevailing direction so much as digesting it.\n\nThe structure story is one of a base built and defended. The 160.60 area stands out as the most significant prior reaction zone in this dataset, having attracted buying interest on four separate occasions. That cluster of demand, sitting just above the 159.87 and 159.44 zones beneath it, forms a layered support shelf that the market has shown no appetite to revisit since early July. Each successive daily close has printed further from that region, and the series of higher lows since the 3 July low near 160.60 constitutes a clean ascending structure. The 163.98 intraday high from 23 July represents the most recent swing high and the immediate overhead reference; price has been consolidating just beneath that level over the past several sessions rather than retreating from it, which the desk reads as constructive behaviour.\n\nOn the hourly chart, the last 24 hours have been characterised by a shallow pullback from the 163.79\u2013163.83 zone printed during the London morning, with price settling back into the 163.71\u2013163.77 range through the early European afternoon. The H1 structure shows no impulsive selling \u2014 the retracements are shallow and orderly, consistent with a pause rather than a reversal. The 163.65\u2013163.70 band, which capped the overnight session before the Asian push higher, now acts as near-term intraday structure support. A sustained hold above this area keeps the hourly picture aligned with the daily bias.\n\nToday's economic calendar carries no scheduled high-impact events, which means price action is likely to remain technically driven for the session. Absent a catalyst, the tight consolidation beneath the 23 July swing high could persist, with any directional resolution more likely to emerge from tomorrow's risk events or broader dollar sentiment shifts.\n\nWhat would change the bullish read? A daily close back beneath the 162.40\u2013162.50 area \u2014 which served as a consolidation ceiling through much of mid-July before giving way \u2014 would introduce doubt about the sustainability of the recent leg higher. A more decisive invalidation would be a return to the 161.30 zone, which marked the lower boundary of the prior consolidation range. Until either of those levels is breached on a closing basis, the structure continues to favour the path of least resistance to the upside.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}